dialogue cohesion_redmage_sage
title: Salve for old burns
trigger: Cohesion redmage sage level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker redmage redmage
speaker sage sage

node open commander
  The Sage has the satchel open and a jar of something green in one hand, and keeps looking at the back of the Red Mage's ungloved hand as if it were a wound still open.
  -> healed

node healed redmage
  They're healed, Sage. Years ago. You can stop measuring them by eye. I can see you doing it.
  -> mended

node mended sage
  Healed isn't the same as mended. That skin's tight as a drum. It pulls when you make a fist, doesn't it? This jar won't take the marks away, but it'll give you your grip back.
  -> stare

node stare redmage
  I did these to myself. On purpose. I'm not sure I want good salve spent on them. Commander, tell the Sage to put the lid back on.
  * Let the Sage tend them. Tonight, the glove stays off. -> tend
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 10
    do: AddTrust redmage -3
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:salve_tended
  * Trade. The Red Mage warms the Sage's jars on cold mornings. The Sage keeps the hand supple. -> trade
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 6
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:salve_traded
  * Scars are the Red Mage's own business. Put the jar away. -> away
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage -4
    do: AddTrust sage -2
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:salve_away
  * The aunt asked the Red Mage to stop, for the Red Mage's own sake. Let the Sage finish what she asked. -> aunt
    if: FlagSet redmage:test_questioned
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 8
    do: AddTrust redmage 2
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:salve_aunt

node tend sage
  Hold still. Cold first, then it warms. You of all people will feel the turn. There. Make a fist. Slowly.
  -> doors

node trade redmage
  Warm jars. That I can do without thinking. Your salves set like candle wax by dawn, Sage. I've watched you chip at them.
  -> doors

node away sage
  Away it goes. I'll leave it at the top of the satchel. Jars don't mind waiting. Healers do, but we're used to it.
  -> doors

node aunt redmage
  She did ask. For my sake. Not because it hurt, because she could see me hoping. Go on, then, Sage. Before I think better of it.
  -> doors

node doors sage
  Your aunt went Hollow at the tithe. Wick's colour went thin in the city, a little more each week. Same Choir, I think. Different doors. I don't know what to do with that, Red Mage. Do you?
  * We promised to bring Wick down. The aunt comes into that promise too. -> promise
    if: FlagSet sage:wick_promised
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 10
    do: AddTrust sage 2
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:doors_promise
  * The coal goes home to the aunt's hearth. The Sage walks it there with the Red Mage. -> hearth
    if: FlagSet redmage:fire_home
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 8
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:doors_hearth
  * Compare everything. Every jar the Sage tried, every night the Red Mage tried. Two lists are better than one. -> lists
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 8
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:doors_lists
  * Different doors. Don't make one grief out of two. -> apart
    do: AddCohesion redmage sage 2
    do: SetFlag redmage_sage:doors_apart

node promise redmage
  The same promise. Wick and her both. That's a bigger stair than it was this morning, Sage. Good. I wanted a reason to climb faster.
  -> close

node hearth sage
  The hearth. I'd like to meet a coal that's outlasted every jar in this satchel. And the person who lit it.
  -> close

node lists redmage
  Every night. I can give you every night. How much heat, how long, what she said. I never wrote any of it down. I remember all of it.
  -> close

node apart sage
  Two griefs. You're right. I'd only have made yours fit the shape of mine. That's a healer's worst habit.
  -> close

node close commander
  The jar ends up open on the stone between them. The Red Mage holds it near the fire until the salve goes soft, and passes it back without being asked.
